  // and the item's normalised unit at the time of writing (kept for history).
  locationId     String?
  unitCode       String?
  // Mapping fields (PC-3). `basis` records which of quantity, amount and
  // weight the user typed; the other two are derived from the item, so a rate
  // change can re-derive a draft without guessing which figure was meant.
  // Legacy rows default to amount, the figure EV and IPC always read.
  // `suggestedBy` and `confidence` are the provenance of a suggestion that
  // became a row (ai, rule:code, rule:wbs, rule:location, rule:name,
  // rule:costcode, import); `importBatchId` lets a mapping-file import be
  // undone as a unit; `supersededByAllocationId` is the audit chain when a
  // row is replaced rather than edited.
  basis                    String    @default("amount") // quantity, amount, weight
